<title>USA: U.S. DAP lower in rail market, ammonia unchanged.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP lower in rail market, ammonia unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diammonium phosphate prices in Florida rail markets were lower Monday as cooperatives dropped prices to attract customers, a cash source said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a competitive thing,&quot; said one dealer. &quot;They're just bidding for business.&quot;</p>
<p>Cash values for ammonia and DAP at the U.S. Gulf were unchanged, dealers said.</p>
<p>			     Dlrs/short ton   Chg from Friday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla		168		     dn 4</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf	  186		     unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		175		     unc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
